": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "without", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610170413 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/6b4d617df080cef71cd8f4b041601cf47ce0edf3/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\nSix bugs, all clear. Fixing them now.\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nI did the three reads you asked for first, then fixed the code. `python3 -m unittest` now passes all 16 tests. Before, it ran 15, because the search tests couldn't even be imported.\n\n**The reads:**\n- **(a)** The `catalog/` directory holds `__init__.py`, `books.py`, `factory.py`, `fees.py`, `inventory.py`, `members.py`, `search.py` and `text.py`.\n- **(b)** Offset 0, limit 5 returned lines 1\u20135: the docstring through `def __init__`.\n- **(c)** Offset 3, limit 5 returned lines 4\u20138. So offset 0 and offset 1 both start at line 1, and offset 3 starts at line 4, not line 3 as a 0-based offset would suggest.\n\n**The fixes (no test files changed):**\n- `catalog/books.py:22`: the year was being kept as text. `parse_book` now converts it to a number, which also fixes `age()`.\n- `catalog/factory.py`: added `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)` so the sample has the three books its docstring describes.\n- `catalog/fees.py:14`: the late fee added the daily rate instead of multiplying by it. Changed `days_late + DAILY_FEE` to `days_late * DAILY_FEE`.\n- `catalog/inventory.py`: `recent(n)` returned one event too many. It now returns the last `n`, and an empty list when `n <= 0`.\n- `catalog/members.py`: the borrow limit was 3, but the comment and tests say 5. Changed `MAX_BORROWED` to 5.\n- `catalog/search.py`: the import pointed at a module that doesn't exist (`catalog.nonexistent`). It now imports `normalize` from `catalog.text`.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": ["param:temperature"], "params_stripped_requests": 1, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 8, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 45521, "requests_cache_write": 66654, "requests_cost_usd": 0.3986382, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 16, "requests_output": 2810, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-read-edge:claude-opus-5-5:trial3", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 245, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-18T07:25:44.152459+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 33.268, "t_checker_s": 0.174, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-read-edge", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "vendor_split", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 2826, "tokens_cache_read": 45521, "tokens_cache_write": 66654, "tokens_fresh": 2807, "tokens_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_main_cache_read": 44489, "tokens_main_cache_write": 66654, "tokens_main_calls": 5, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 12, "tokens_main_output": 2795, "tokens_output": 2810, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 45521, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 66654, "tokens_proxy_calls": 6, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_proxy_output": 2810, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "toolchain": {"ai": "5.0.124", "anthropic": "2.